  "_fixture_note": "Solver-catches seed (experiment 011, assume-guarantee-order). The adjudicating experiment the professor and language-team agreed on: an in-fragment (QF-LIA + arrays) task where a WRONG CALL ORDER passes a blind test but the solver refutes a withheld call-pre. Given: `guard` (ensures the account's value is non-negative: post map-has result k AND >= 0) and `consume` (its VISIBLE pre is only map-has; its body is identity). The agent fills `process-body` to prepare then consume the account. GRADER-GAP INVARIANT: consume's REAL precondition (the value must be non-negative) is WITHHELD \u2014 hidden-specs/011.json strengthens consume's pre to (and (map-has m k) (>= (map-get m k) 0)), injected onto consume at grade time, and process is re-verified. refuted = a fill that calls consume before guarding (so consume's non-negativity call-pre is unmet on a negative-balance input the solver quantifies over) = grade A; verified = guard-then-consume, the call-pre discharged by guard's post = grade B; vacuous = C. The visible check samples a POSITIVE balance (k=5), where consume's weak visible pre holds for either order, so a wrong-order fill passes it (tests blind); only the solver, via the withheld non-negativity call-pre, catches the ordering. process carries an anchor post (map-has result k, weak, non-discriminating) so its body VC \u2014 and thus the consume call-pre obligation \u2014 is emitted (a naive anchorless map-returning body falls back, LLMLL.md \u00a75.3.4). Straight-line at the store level; sidesteps the F-011.3 conditional-store residue. Stripped by prepare_run.py::_strip_fixture_metadata on copytree.",
